			},
			"text": "Heritage roofing slate: the cast concrete photograph cleaned as white-stone is, tinted blue-grey (Beige), cut into slates six across and nine up a repeat in broken courses (Cladding: at 12 units a repeat, slates 2 by 1.3) with a shade of their own each (PanelTone) and a shadow line under each course (JointShade), which JointNormal sinks into the softened photograph's normal map. Non-metallic. Lay it with the courses level, across the slope.",
			"title": "Slate",
			"type": "comment"
